schema: "0.4"
id: trd-nav-concept-d-synthesis
type: image
quality: high
service: gemini

prompt:
  text: >
    Professional macOS desktop application UI mockup for a 3D UML modeling tool,
    synthesis layout: native macOS menu bar at very top (File, Edit, Model,
    Diagram, View, Window, Help); below it a slim dark context toolbar with a
    centered segmented mode switcher (Select | Connect | Place) plus a
    relationship-type dropdown and camera and layout icon buttons on the right;
    left side an expanded model browser panel showing a file tree, a diagram list
    with small kind badges (class, sequence, ERD) and a Recents section, with a
    narrow icon rail at its left edge for collapsing it; right side a tall dark
    inspector panel with collapsible sections and form fields (Name, Stereotype,
    Package, Attributes); bottom a thin status strip with breadcrumb path, mode
    indicator, camera coordinates; center a large dark 3D viewport with floating
    UML class boxes connected by glowing cyan relationship lines in perspective
    over a subtle grid floor; a small translucent floating contextual toolbar
    hovers beside one selected glowing class box with tiny connect/edit/delete
    icons; a translucent spotlight-style command palette bar floats top-center of
    the viewport reading "Type a command". Dark charcoal theme, single cyan-teal
    accent, crisp 1px borders, flat minimal professional design, Unity-editor-like
    dockable panel headers, macOS aesthetic. Clean legible UI labels.
  negative: "photograph, hands, people, watermark, blurry text, light theme, purple, detached floating windows outside app frame"
  style: ui-mockup

output:
  formats:
    - format: png
      quality: 100
  dimensions:
    width: 1600
    height: 900
    aspect_ratio: "16:9"

tags: [trd, ui, nav-redesign, concept-d, synthesis]
